[{:db/id "q-351724/field-1/8f25caad3f6e1433d6bf48b82f652fd7635528b467283364db6b4153fad3f18d" :answer/id #uuid "eb7675da-3715-50c7-8e7e-0edb9d8056e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1-\\cot(t)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351724/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f6a8c2fc-1baf-5461-8089-f41525dae5c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351724/field-1/8f25caad3f6e1433d6bf48b82f652fd7635528b467283364db6b4153fad3f18d" :answer-field/choices ["q-351724/field-1/8f25caad3f6e1433d6bf48b82f652fd7635528b467283364db6b4153fad3f18d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351724" :question/id #uuid "d598999c-b003-52da-8100-10acae05a1ed" :question/math-academy-id "q-351724" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)={csc}^{2}⁡(t),$ where $t>0$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=0$ when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t.$\n\n$x(t)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int {csc}^{2}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(t)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $x(\\frac{\\pi }{4})=0.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})+C \\\\ 0 & =-1+C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=-\\operatorname{cot}⁡(t)+1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-351724/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c234eb8-4a5b-52e1-8854-c183b68184bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351724"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7283/selection/335b50a9aa32f312a500d59b5bdeff94dc791be7f3f72529907305438ca2eba1" :answer/id #uuid "153b7060-1af7-5df8-8386-280aa2d65270" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={t}^{3}+{t}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7283/selection/51ee73e5d59b1ec74dc2e202a79f2f61d9f291d659ab55673e284594fe5e5e05" :answer/id #uuid "b1cd59fe-630b-55eb-8393-a803f40c26a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=4t+7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7283/selection/0e173bc532ea2100e1e84c38bf951b00adab273e883f1a377048c1ff2fe45500" :answer/id #uuid "aa5ac2ba-8edd-51a5-b31a-0a77e30bebb7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={t}^{3}+{t}^{2}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7283/selection/58684a41fc868e30a38ee336faef0f7f4fa7ab1d507d0ae5e600626d80bb07e0" :answer/id #uuid "cc07f719-7fb0-5ccc-a345-3d7a9e10665d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=6t+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7283/selection/99745bb93ff9b270082a643b0611606db3619362d25a190144b397024f3d4369" :answer/id #uuid "d334e6f8-69dd-59fc-9e62-60d42cdd6b5a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={t}^{3}+{t}^{2}-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7283/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0ddf3d81-e826-57d4-8134-c53e47130c3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-7283/selection/0e173bc532ea2100e1e84c38bf951b00adab273e883f1a377048c1ff2fe45500" :answer-field/choices ["q-7283/selection/335b50a9aa32f312a500d59b5bdeff94dc791be7f3f72529907305438ca2eba1" "q-7283/selection/51ee73e5d59b1ec74dc2e202a79f2f61d9f291d659ab55673e284594fe5e5e05" "q-7283/selection/0e173bc532ea2100e1e84c38bf951b00adab273e883f1a377048c1ff2fe45500" "q-7283/selection/58684a41fc868e30a38ee336faef0f7f4fa7ab1d507d0ae5e600626d80bb07e0" "q-7283/selection/99745bb93ff9b270082a643b0611606db3619362d25a190144b397024f3d4369"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7283" :question/id #uuid "fdf1d19a-20e1-526f-8082-40001a3f405c" :question/math-academy-id "q-7283" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=3{t}^{2}+2t,$ where $t$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=15$ when $t=2,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t>0.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (3{t}^{2}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={t}^{3}+{t}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $x(2)=15.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}15 & =(2)^{3}+(2)^{2}+C \\\\ 15 & =8+4+C \\\\ C & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{3}+{t}^{2}+3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7283/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c234eb8-4a5b-52e1-8854-c183b68184bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7283"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-6255/selection/585a766c0f34cba96b1cfdbaf7ac1c4dba14e7bb897024850423bc61bf589d5f" :answer/id #uuid "4c6bb769-15ed-5ef1-9fd1-b892437d6769" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={t}^{4}+{t}^{2}+6t-\\frac{20}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6255/selection/3dc3e2dcf90fb178c12e8d958b4185670f83fd7d0e054b62598d1a6709e4de5c" :answer/id #uuid "fda4b7f1-5fc0-5fc4-aa86-a0c8d5bd0d79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=4{t}^{3}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+6t+\\frac{20}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6255/selection/6115c9da8630b949323ba9140ef1b275ebd498f88175bbae397582201da91739" :answer/id #uuid "2e129c55-9fa8-5b4e-846b-7cc3246ac7af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={t}^{4}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+3{t}^{2}+\\frac{20}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6255/selection/c334b669999cd002746f6ef207a1c50356c915e99da5babbf24d15dff0432954" :answer/id #uuid "2e15f3fd-5fe0-57f4-91cc-df909c37fa20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=4{t}^{3}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+3{t}^{2}+\\frac{20}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6255/selection/e506797cf8962bb9e525fc855816e56a6b705a0b6d4dd6b9539cc08d259acd82" :answer/id #uuid "7681f6e8-66b9-5711-ae05-3ec0c6c21856" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={t}^{4}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+3{t}^{2}-\\frac{20}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-6255/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "beacb1b4-e6ff-5b29-848e-cb0c8fe781e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-6255/selection/6115c9da8630b949323ba9140ef1b275ebd498f88175bbae397582201da91739" :answer-field/choices ["q-6255/selection/585a766c0f34cba96b1cfdbaf7ac1c4dba14e7bb897024850423bc61bf589d5f" "q-6255/selection/3dc3e2dcf90fb178c12e8d958b4185670f83fd7d0e054b62598d1a6709e4de5c" "q-6255/selection/6115c9da8630b949323ba9140ef1b275ebd498f88175bbae397582201da91739" "q-6255/selection/c334b669999cd002746f6ef207a1c50356c915e99da5babbf24d15dff0432954" "q-6255/selection/e506797cf8962bb9e525fc855816e56a6b705a0b6d4dd6b9539cc08d259acd82"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-6255" :question/id #uuid "47fb04f1-6892-5e82-9539-204f7e5c883c" :question/math-academy-id "q-6255" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=4{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}+6t,$ where $t$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=11$ when $t=1,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t>0.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,dt \\\\  & =\\int (4{t}^{3}+{t}^{2}+6t)dt \\\\  & ={t}^{4}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+3{t}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $x(1)=11.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}11 & =(1)^{4}+\\frac{(1)^{3}}{3}+3(1)^{2}+C \\\\ 11 & =1+\\frac{1}{3}+3+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{20}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{4}+\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+3{t}^{2}+\\frac{20}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-6255/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c234eb8-4a5b-52e1-8854-c183b68184bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-6255"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7284/selection/7759fee804b5d5962e55b9f8f9d649c027bd06bdef1c3d01ae406096e50a9fef" :answer/id #uuid "5f6e578b-a181-58fb-bb19-8e8b2aaad005" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7284/selection/587e4c54cc1eeb66f8b676c2863ed3e7ecf745e4592316c1ee9fb351292228f3" :answer/id #uuid "883ca621-8638-5983-a96d-4fe709aa8112" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+\\frac{7}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7284/selection/3ec1a8880158020ef1b94443c1fd448e2a354aacc79b89077e6089587ec3dada" :answer/id #uuid "a8631ccd-4695-50b3-8a92-be83b8e2d24f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7284/selection/2d1292b85d4967d2b3a430ad0441d86c2893a4892d4e5357db51a1bfc42e3a11" :answer/id #uuid "f4ceefa5-decf-57a6-b7a0-0c434c1bee25" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}-\\frac{63}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7284/selection/b162713f99087c25080cd1ec1f034ea99a787b5d34a3097c2d00a6bb47d16444" :answer/id #uuid "d9bb6baa-db02-5570-86e1-600085365d37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{4}-2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7284/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8acd796b-65df-53ad-8fea-bf76684284d3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-7284/selection/587e4c54cc1eeb66f8b676c2863ed3e7ecf745e4592316c1ee9fb351292228f3" :answer-field/choices ["q-7284/selection/7759fee804b5d5962e55b9f8f9d649c027bd06bdef1c3d01ae406096e50a9fef" "q-7284/selection/587e4c54cc1eeb66f8b676c2863ed3e7ecf745e4592316c1ee9fb351292228f3" "q-7284/selection/3ec1a8880158020ef1b94443c1fd448e2a354aacc79b89077e6089587ec3dada" "q-7284/selection/2d1292b85d4967d2b3a430ad0441d86c2893a4892d4e5357db51a1bfc42e3a11" "q-7284/selection/b162713f99087c25080cd1ec1f034ea99a787b5d34a3097c2d00a6bb47d16444"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7284" :question/id #uuid "7529948b-5a79-5722-a1f5-bf453f077a49" :question/math-academy-id "q-7284" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=\\frac{1}{4}t-{t}^{2},$ where $t>0$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=-7$ when $t=3,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{4}t-{t}^{2})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $x(3)=-7.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7 & =\\frac{1}{8}(3)^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}(3)^{3}+C \\\\ -7 & =-\\frac{63}{8}+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{7}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{1}{8}{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+\\frac{7}{8}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-7284/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0c234eb8-4a5b-52e1-8854-c183b68184bd"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7284"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-7110"] :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t)=6t+6{t}^{2},$ where $t>0$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=2$ when $t=0,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (6t+6{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C$, we use the fact that $x(0)=2.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =3(0)^{2}+2(0)^{3}+C \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=3{t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}+2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-351730/field-1/c546e5583f0245c2db8abcc6571a598c92afd7f0f1ef4635f5464fea7c44eb38" :answer/id #uuid "f16f387d-edce-54ee-8767-0b82d1c97ee7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^{3t}}{9}+\\frac{2t}{3}-\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351730/field-1/ff3d15f1a06d7009ae72d1b70b4ccdc0a377d0bf489005034baed5762abb4c12" :answer/id #uuid "19414c18-04a3-56f6-849d-f4dca4fd12ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e^{3t}}{9}+\\frac{2t}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351730/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d25ac9b8-b806-565e-8499-3284b9f5ebcc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351730/field-1/c546e5583f0245c2db8abcc6571a598c92afd7f0f1ef4635f5464fea7c44eb38" :answer-field/choices ["q-351730/field-1/c546e5583f0245c2db8abcc6571a598c92afd7f0f1ef4635f5464fea7c44eb38" "q-351730/field-1/ff3d15f1a06d7009ae72d1b70b4ccdc0a377d0bf489005034baed5762abb4c12"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351730" :question/id #uuid "273d6d87-8669-5f51-96f8-3d528dae9efc" :question/math-academy-id "q-351730" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t)={e}^{3t},$ where $t\\ge 0$ is the time. If the particle has position $x=0$ and velocity $v=1$ when $t=0,$ the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is\n\n$x(t)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the acceleration to get the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int {e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $v(0)=1.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{0}+C \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{3}+C \\\\ C & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is given by $v(t)=\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}+\\frac{2}{3}.$\n\nNow, we integrate the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{3t}+\\frac{2}{3})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{3t}\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{2}{3}\\int \\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3t}+\\frac{2}{3}t+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $K$, we use the fact that $x(0)=0.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{0}+\\frac{2}{3}(0)+K \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{9}+K \\\\ K & =-\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{1}{9}{e}^{3t}+\\frac{2}{3}t-\\frac{1}{9}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-351730/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43e68991-37f0-543e-a4da-b78b395a8494"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351730"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-81441/selection/4ff2acadcb514e260ceb93c90abd39c98081133442574038eddcfa778c432a6d" :answer/id #uuid "53fb6580-320e-5947-9b68-c2238cf9f2d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=t+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81441/selection/8f5b5b69ffa3b8b87007908c1426783a81c4a7183b8a37d21a79afb26d42c1ca" :answer/id #uuid "97336569-bc9a-5185-837d-0317e9002304" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=2t-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81441/selection/5497a9ee5b3540116435ee76634a01b1496edf99cb5dc3b1a3ef36892ea5e664" :answer/id #uuid "f2480a20-1cea-56e1-a6c2-24ac3c7b1ec5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=2t-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81441/selection/168b6e07f389134c339954a6ab4ad9ee617d246ccec6cadfdea645647a567e9f" :answer/id #uuid "d6547d14-3742-5628-9104-81391c0682e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81441/selection/9c71f05402af0bf6c5df9e2508139c61532594f0db0544a35abbed4308761435" :answer/id #uuid "fb9c4b90-9108-58d3-88c0-ef8beab10393" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=2t+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-81441/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "194a0fc3-e330-575c-85b7-ba6b49b567d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-81441/selection/8f5b5b69ffa3b8b87007908c1426783a81c4a7183b8a37d21a79afb26d42c1ca" :answer-field/choices ["q-81441/selection/4ff2acadcb514e260ceb93c90abd39c98081133442574038eddcfa778c432a6d" "q-81441/selection/8f5b5b69ffa3b8b87007908c1426783a81c4a7183b8a37d21a79afb26d42c1ca" "q-81441/selection/5497a9ee5b3540116435ee76634a01b1496edf99cb5dc3b1a3ef36892ea5e664" "q-81441/selection/168b6e07f389134c339954a6ab4ad9ee617d246ccec6cadfdea645647a567e9f" "q-81441/selection/9c71f05402af0bf6c5df9e2508139c61532594f0db0544a35abbed4308761435"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-81441" :question/id #uuid "d0b98d95-03af-598a-9e95-71e4d8b5a534" :question/math-academy-id "q-81441" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t),$ where $t\\ge 0$ is the time. If the particle has position $x=5$ and velocity $v=1$ when $t=0,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the acceleration to get the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $v(0)=1.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3(0))+C \\\\ 1 & =-1+C \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is given by $v(t)=2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t).$\n\nNow, we integrate the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (2-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t))\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2t-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $K,$ we use the fact that $x(0)=5.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5 & =2(0)-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3(0))+K \\\\ K & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=2t-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-81441/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43e68991-37f0-543e-a4da-b78b395a8494"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-81441"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7111/selection/892f208af8eea157de11b9beea3fee73544a31c25c6beb3e9669a25b0fc22104" :answer/id #uuid "b5d1caed-313e-5978-a848-16b8e6ea03d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={t}^{2}+{t}^{3}+4t+2." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7111/selection/fa6cb98827160e9615756b0bbfd66a5acf33047413a1f69dd779a823c5514933" :answer/id #uuid "ae20499b-c11b-5052-83f0-daa09f68f7e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-{t}^{3}+6t." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7111/selection/f776302595fda5586cf490b74eac82fc2e0f7dcba78c98316dd107c21b7ef318" :answer/id #uuid "25055ab8-5116-58f3-870f-cb322f8954e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={t}^{2}-{t}^{3}+2t+2." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7111/selection/6053b321a849e9db4683ac55e620686f017d25495343128e04988a40abec69bc" :answer/id #uuid "b109b242-4d91-5866-b06c-c0c243684404" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}+{t}^{3}+6t-2." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7111/selection/2414cf3a4158c48e87db83496d17636cfe71f028e9558d206f68a0e767c026da" :answer/id #uuid "283c4063-e17d-59d7-b05f-3aeab7b48772" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-{t}^{3}+4t+2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7111/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff3680c8-8c21-5564-bf81-58067a900364" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-7111/selection/2414cf3a4158c48e87db83496d17636cfe71f028e9558d206f68a0e767c026da" :answer-field/choices ["q-7111/selection/892f208af8eea157de11b9beea3fee73544a31c25c6beb3e9669a25b0fc22104" "q-7111/selection/fa6cb98827160e9615756b0bbfd66a5acf33047413a1f69dd779a823c5514933" "q-7111/selection/f776302595fda5586cf490b74eac82fc2e0f7dcba78c98316dd107c21b7ef318" "q-7111/selection/6053b321a849e9db4683ac55e620686f017d25495343128e04988a40abec69bc" "q-7111/selection/2414cf3a4158c48e87db83496d17636cfe71f028e9558d206f68a0e767c026da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-7111" :question/id #uuid "13736185-7d14-5f0f-bf06-55c5bf19c2a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-7111" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t)=1-6t,$ where $t\\ge 0$ is the time. If the particle has position $x=2$ and velocity $v=4$ when $t=0,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t>0.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the acceleration to get the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (1-6t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =t-3{t}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $v(0)=4.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =(0)-3(0)^{2}+C \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is given by $v(t)=t-3{t}^{2}+4.$\n\nNow, we integrate the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (t-3{t}^{2}+4)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-{t}^{3}+4t+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $K,$ we use the fact that $x(0)=2.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}-(0)^{3}+4(0)+K \\\\ K & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-{t}^{3}+4t+2.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-7111/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43e68991-37f0-543e-a4da-b78b395a8494"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-7111"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351742/field-1/72d6fad4a214a90e34d956232884e392b1b69af0b184c7b38bd42d551f7aab47" :answer/id #uuid "5c85da6b-693e-5b55-8b2b-cb592647c4b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6t^2+t-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351742/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a588a670-231e-5605-95a4-a382ffcf11db" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351742/field-1/72d6fad4a214a90e34d956232884e392b1b69af0b184c7b38bd42d551f7aab47" :answer-field/choices ["q-351742/field-1/72d6fad4a214a90e34d956232884e392b1b69af0b184c7b38bd42d551f7aab47"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351742" :question/id #uuid "af944fef-addc-5ba8-99ae-2326f2684b0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-351742" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t)=20{t}^{3}+12,$ where $t\\ge 0$ is the time. If the particle has position $x=-3$ and velocity $v=1$ when $t=0,$ the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is\n\n$x(t)={t}^{5}+\\,$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the acceleration to get the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (20{t}^{3}+12)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =5{t}^{4}+12t+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $v(0)=1.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =0+0+C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is given by $v(t)=5{t}^{4}+12t+1.$\n\nNow, we integrate the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (5{t}^{4}+12t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={t}^{5}+6{t}^{2}+t+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $K$, we use the fact that $x(0)=-3.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3 & =0+0+0+K \\\\ K & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{5}+6{t}^{2}+t-3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-351742/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43e68991-37f0-543e-a4da-b78b395a8494"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351742"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-84244/selection/00fffb27ac6de1aef17608c054be17619ad193cad8f7b326e0ff51ab13f5c5b8" :answer/id #uuid "fd91ab91-5062-5dbc-8ee3-cbcbdc22bbbb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)-2t+3\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84244/selection/4a46c988f4bae8e6429b240cf5abc7e77707ff3777022296fe2285c5d1ebca6c" :answer/id #uuid "09154eac-a091-51cd-9bcd-01505287cd20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+2t+\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84244/selection/3918716ebc2b4c84baf73e344e4ad4760d19ae2a12131111d0ec4c91f8fee935" :answer/id #uuid "0f998b3e-512e-5a38-9369-447e501d61bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+2t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84244/selection/5c3f247132819112a1a5eec98f59010c0bbd813410259a1b24d8deca8acaa1f4" :answer/id #uuid "3bc75397-04fe-5142-95a6-3d79a59998ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+4t" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84244/selection/eccba684b42c2026f4281aa101ff4dd2ebd58dc1d564e5630030c586bef03fed" :answer/id #uuid "a6831d72-7e48-59cf-9c98-9602655059df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)=-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+2t+\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-84244/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e8f49fdf-2810-54d5-9246-8a3b730d3fdb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-84244/selection/4a46c988f4bae8e6429b240cf5abc7e77707ff3777022296fe2285c5d1ebca6c" :answer-field/choices ["q-84244/selection/00fffb27ac6de1aef17608c054be17619ad193cad8f7b326e0ff51ab13f5c5b8" "q-84244/selection/4a46c988f4bae8e6429b240cf5abc7e77707ff3777022296fe2285c5d1ebca6c" "q-84244/selection/3918716ebc2b4c84baf73e344e4ad4760d19ae2a12131111d0ec4c91f8fee935" "q-84244/selection/5c3f247132819112a1a5eec98f59010c0bbd813410259a1b24d8deca8acaa1f4" "q-84244/selection/eccba684b42c2026f4281aa101ff4dd2ebd58dc1d564e5630030c586bef03fed"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-84244" :question/id #uuid "641e7b63-702c-540a-b9fd-6b417e1a8c11" :question/math-academy-id "q-84244" :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t),$ where $t\\ge 0$ is the time. If the particle has position $x=2\\pi $ and velocity $v=4$ when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the acceleration to get the velocity $v(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $v(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=4.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4 & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+C \\\\ 4 & =2(1)+C \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is given by $v(t)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+2.$\n\nNow, we integrate the velocity to get $x(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)+2)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+2t+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $K,$ we use the fact that $x(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=2\\pi .$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\pi  & =-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+2(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+K \\\\ 2\\pi  & =-2(0)+\\pi +K \\\\ K & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t)=-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)+2t+\\pi .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-84244/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43e68991-37f0-543e-a4da-b78b395a8494"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-84244"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-566"] :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with velocity $v(t) = 2t+3t^2,$ where $t\\geq 0$ is the time. If the particle is at the position $x=1$ when $t=0,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the velocity to get $x(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (2t+3{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={t}^{2}+{t}^{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $x(0) = 1.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =(0)^{2}+(0)^{3}+C \\\\ C & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is\n\n$$\nx(t) = t^3+t^2+1.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-567"] :question/problem "A particle moves along a straight line relative to a fixed origin $O$ with acceleration $a(t) = 1-2t,$ where $t\\geq 0$ is the time. If the particle has position $x=1$ and velocity $v=2$ when $t=1,$ calculate the position $x$ of the particle at time $t >0.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by integrating the acceleration to get the velocity $v(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v(t) & =\\int a(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (1-2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =t-{t}^{2}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $C,$ we use the fact that $v(1) = 2.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =(1)-(1)^{2}+C \\\\ C & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the velocity is given by $v(t) = t-t^2 + 2.$\n\nNow, we integrate the velocity to get $x(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & =\\int v(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int (t-{t}^{2}+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}{t}^{3}+2t+K\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo determine $K,$ we use the fact that $x(1) = 1.$ Substituting this into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{1}{2}(1)^{2}-\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3}+2(1)+K \\\\ K & =-\\frac{7}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position $x$ of the particle at time $t$ is \n\n$$\nx(t) = \\dfrac{1}{2}t^2-\\dfrac{1}{3}t^3 +2t -\\dfrac{7}{6}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
